# belt/sheaths/dagger: the dagger sheathed on the left hip (`sheath dagger`: P2C_CONTRACTS 3; STYLE_P2 11: "the dagger at
# the hip"), P2c wave 2 WEAPONS. A3's scabbard in small: a 5 px leather sheath (dark outline, lit left, a steel chape)
# hung from the belt, the dagger's brass guard and pommel and its grip above the throat; drawn: the empty sheath, its
# mouth dark. Where the sword's scabbard hangs (belt/sheaths/sword), shorter, so the off hand on the hilt reads the same.
# Facing right it hangs behind the body (the far hip, layer back); facing left in front. Sheath channel: rest kick lag
# drawn sit stride; lie draws nothing. Hip anchor. Finish regions: R the guard and pommel, G the pommel.
use person
body adult
role sheath dagger
layer belt
anchor hip
keys sheath

